    {
      "id": "kpk1-l21-d1-t01",
      "before": "kpk1-l21-d1-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "Robiłam czy zrobiłam?"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Most Polish verbs come in pairs. The imperfective one, *robić*, *czytać*, shows an action as a process or a habit: *wczoraj długo czytałam*, yesterday I was reading for a long time. The perfective one, *zrobić*, *przeczytać*, shows one action done to the end, with a result: *przeczytałam książkę*, I read the book, I finished it. Often the perfective is the same verb with a prefix: *robić* and *zrobić*, *czytać* and *przeczytać*."
      }
    }
  ],
